WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.382
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Saturday, November seventh.

2
00:00:04.382 --> 00:00:07.293
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:11.911
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.440
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:23.338
UK maritime authorities have reported another tanker explosion in the Strait of Hormuz, and a ship manager says a seafarer died in this week's tanker strike north of Qatar.

6
00:00:23.338 --> 00:00:30.017
The US Mission in Saudi Arabia has issued a new security alert as Houthi missile and drone fire continues.

7
00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:35.244
And Europe's hoax bomb threats have spread from flights to newsrooms.

8
00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:36.488
Here's the detail.

9
00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:39.506
Gulf shipping.

10
00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:52.982
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations, warning one ninety-seven: a time-late report of an explosion at the waterline of a tanker sailing outbound through the Strait of Hormuz, about sixteen nautical miles off northern Oman, on Thursday afternoon, Central time.

11
00:00:52.982 --> 00:00:58.627
The crew are safe and the ship continued its voyage.

12
00:00:58.627 --> 00:01:02.247
UKMTO did not state a cause, and calls this a time-late report; reporting can lag.

13
00:01:02.247 --> 00:01:11.950
Separately, the Greek manager of a product tanker says one seafarer was killed in an explosion it believes was caused by a missile while the ship was sailing toward Bahrain.

14
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:18.919
Philippine officials say the seafarer was Filipino and a second Filipino crew member was injured.

15
00:01:18.919 --> 00:01:20.117
That is reported.

16
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:26.120
Maritime media identify it as the tanker struck north of Qatar this week; UKMTO has not named the vessel.

17
00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:31.306
Iran's navy also claims another tanker hit a mine in the eastern Strait on Saturday.

18
00:01:31.306 --> 00:01:35.999
That is a claim only, with no matching UKMTO warning so far.

19
00:01:35.999 --> 00:01:43.384
The latest joint maritime centre assessment still rates the Strait of Hormuz severe and the wider Arabian Gulf substantial.

20
00:01:43.384 --> 00:01:51.424
Tueri suggests operators review crew welfare and routing plans for Gulf voyages, and treat unmatched claims as unconfirmed.

21
00:01:51.424 --> 00:01:52.814
Saudi Arabia.

22
00:01:52.814 --> 00:02:04.344
Confirmed: the US Mission issued a security alert on Saturday urging heightened vigilance because of the increased threat of Houthi attacks and Iranian efforts to target US government officials in the region.

23
00:02:04.344 --> 00:02:12.646
It warns of possible flight cancellations and airspace closures, and says land borders, including the causeway to Bahrain, remain open.

24
00:02:12.646 --> 00:02:24.437
Reported, through the Saudi-led coalition: a Houthi cruise missile aimed at the Riyadh region was intercepted on Saturday, after interceptions over the Najran, Riyadh and Mecca regions on Friday.

25
00:02:24.437 --> 00:02:29.165
The Houthi claim of a drone strike on Dammam's airport remains a claim only.

26
00:02:29.165 --> 00:02:40.760
At about two thirty-five p.m. local time today, Flightradar twenty-four showed thirty-six Riyadh cancellations, about seventeen percent, against roughly two hundred fourteen flights on the board.

27
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.423
Bases differ day to day, so no trend can be drawn.

28
00:02:44.423 --> 00:02:51.833
One correction: recent briefs cited the November second alert as the latest; the mission also issued one on November third.

29
00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:58.449
Tueri suggests travelers confirm each flight with the airline and keep a ground route in their contingency plans.

30
00:02:58.449 --> 00:02:59.296
Europe.

31
00:02:59.296 --> 00:03:06.405
Reported: hoax bomb threats again hit flights to and from Lisbon, Rome, Prague and Sofia on Friday, and spread to newsrooms.

32
00:03:06.405 --> 00:03:11.478
Ireland's public broadcaster evacuated its offices.

33
00:03:11.478 --> 00:03:13.470
No explosives have been found.

34
00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:21.690
Separately, the State Department says a general strike is set across Spain on Wednesday, November eleventh, with transport cut to minimum services.

35
00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:27.021
Tueri suggests travelers allow extra time and confirm any Wednesday travel in Spain.

36
00:03:27.021 --> 00:03:28.525
Operations check.

37
00:03:28.525 --> 00:03:37.483
Borders and health, US: the Ebola attestation order remains in force for flights to the United States, with no change on the CDC page.

38
00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.883
No attestation, no boarding.

39
00:03:38.883 --> 00:03:52.287
Borders and health, Nigeria: the US Embassy in Abuja's health alert says all international arrivals are screened, and travelers could be subject to quarantine or self-isolation for at least twenty-one days.

40
00:03:52.287 --> 00:03:54.199
That describes a possibility, not a blanket rule for every arrival.

41
00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:58.987
It has been in place since late October.

42
00:03:58.987 --> 00:04:05.228
Borders and health, Cameroon: Britain's Foreign Office now says arrivals at two international airports may face thermal screening for Ebola.

43
00:04:05.228 --> 00:04:15.802
Borders, Kenya: the Foreign Office now advises against all but essential travel to Moyale town and five kilometres around it, at the Ethiopian border.

44
00:04:15.802 --> 00:04:19.071
Borders, Belize: the thirty-day state of emergency remains in force.

45
00:04:19.071 --> 00:04:22.944
Hazards: Mayon volcano remains at alert level three.

46
00:04:22.944 --> 00:04:25.879
India's weather office expects no depression to form in the next seven days.

47
00:04:25.879 --> 00:04:35.551
Infrastructure: Russian strikes caused new power outages in seven Ukrainian regions, reported via officials.

48
00:04:35.551 --> 00:04:37.186
That's today's brief.

49
00:04:37.186 --> 00:04:38.604
Current as of six a.m.

50
00:04:38.604 --> 00:04:41.444
Central, Saturday.

51
00:04:41.444 --> 00:04:43.881
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

52
00:04:43.881 --> 00:04:48.424
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

53
00:04:48.424 --> 00:04:50.809
Check the original source before you act.

54
00:04:50.809 --> 00:04:59.733
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

55
00:04:59.733 --> 00:05:02.412
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

56
00:05:02.412 --> 00:05:03.728
Thanks for listening.
